Bug fix: replace unsafe ArraySchema type casts with ForEachable<T> interface.

This commit modifies 1 file (+27/-12 lines), touching 1 networking file.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
The Colyseus ArraySchema<T> type is not assignable to T[], but supports
.forEach(). Instead of `as unknown as T[]` double-casts, introduce a
ForEachable<T> interface that captures the actual usage pattern. This
eliminates all unsafe casts in convertState() while preserving the
performance optimization of passing ArraySchema objects directly
(avoiding Array.from() copies at 30Hz).
